			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863661">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes, however critique is welcomed.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama / Story</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> An SCP article which is formed as more of a narrative, with reoccurring updates to the SCP itself's sheet. (Think SCP-5000.)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An unexplained (yet theorized) scientific phenomena referred to as &quot;Earthquake lights&quot;. Strange lights that seem to appear in the skies whilst (usually high-magnitude) earthquakes form. However, what isn't expected is that these are entities made of light, appearing to simply spectate the earthquakes. Why they do this is found out in the tale.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> During a high-magnitude earthquake near Site [REDACTED], there were &quot;Earthquake Lights&quot; spotted by many people. As this is a scientifically unexplained phenomena, MTF Unit Rho-10 &quot;Shaken, Not Stirred&quot; (an MTF unit created to withstand seismic activity, or unnatural geological movement) enters the scene to investigate. After recordings are taken, and the film is placed through numerous filters &amp; intensive analyzation, it's found that each of these 'strobes' of light contain an indescribable entity seemingly of extreme brightness (think a Lovecraftian entity), which just so happens to be entity an which seems to be watching the earthquakes. When another high-magnitude earthquake occurs near the same area within the next month, the same dispatch is sent to investigate these flashes of light closer.<br />
As the protagonist, code-name &quot;Charlie-0&quot; (or C-0 by military alphabets) approaches towards the light, it seems to remain still for much longer than previous. They go to the top of the nearest destroyed building via an extremely long grappling hook and a lot of climbing. 23 minutes later, they arrive at the top, before the entity slowly floats down towards him. They take him somewhere - yet to be discovered. The man would slowly begin to communicate with these entities, finding out more and more about them - as the secrets reveal he continually updates the logs manually. The MTF Unit shows development by originally only interacting with the entities for research purposes, however slowly grows to empathize with the fact that they regret their nature. These entities don't wish to create and spectate the chaos which happens, however as if an addiction they depend on it. It is unknown whether they die if there is no chaos spectated. He empathizes, as he was originally a drug addict who severely struggled to break his addiction. He gains motivation to learn more about them to try and find a way to have the foundation assist in this 'chaos'-addiction, as that's what he always wished he had. This also motivates him to write more so the foundation can understand as much as they can.<br />
These light creatures are entities born from dying stars, and as such are naturally attracted towards extremely chaotic events, living off of the chaos. Due to the fact that it's one of the few places which are inhabited, these entities seem to enjoy the chaos which comes with this. When times are extremely boring, they seem to create their own manual disasters, usually by moving tectonic plates and creating earthquakes. as they're the easiest to create.<br />
After they allow him to leave, he goes to the SCP Foundation with all the logged knowledge, discussion, and updates to the file, explaining everything he's learnt (almost everything there is to know). By the end, the SCP Foundation sends him back as a sort of 'messenger' to attempt to create a peace treaty. After this offering for peace, the SCPs seem to at first oblige. For the next year there are no earthquake lights spectated. However, they seem to continue after this time - seemingly more severe then previously, as if something of a relapse. This'd be a whole 'nother stress for the foundation, and I'd need to choose what they'd do after this. As they're aware they would be unable to defeat these entities, the most they can do is attempt to lower the amount of damage caused by SCP-XXXX-1 related earthquakes, and cover up the phenomena as something which it is not.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The fact that this could, hypothetically, be real is a big thing. Playing off of real world unexplained phenomena. Not to mention the fact it opens up as a tale-SCP has always caught my interest. Another main hook is the fact that these creatures seem to have a society, and people they care about, along with emotions and feeling. It gives a side to them other than just 'chaos-lovers'.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> There is almost definitely some shit which I've messed up with the lore, as I am an idiot. Please feel free to be harsh in critique. Thank you!</p>
