<p>Thank you for responding!</p>
<p>I intend for the MTF unit to originally only stay there to gain more Intel, however slowly come to learn that it's actually an entire race of people which are seemingly god-like. The reason they took him is because he's the first non-light entity to attempt to interact with them in all of history. Of course they know about humans, but not much as they only seem to watch earthquakes or other catastrophic events such as Volcanoes and the like.<br />
He'd slowly figure out most of the information due to inference and suggestion from the entities.<br />
While I haven't directly decided on this 100%, I've been considering the fact that these SCPs are actually revealed to manually move tectonic plates to cause earthquakes, which would be extremely dangerous if they're capable of doing that.<br />
I was considering that due to the nature of the SCPs extreme difficulty to contain and high danger, the SCP Foundation could possibly attempt to even attack the entities whilst they're appearing during an earthquake to neutralize the threat of extreme magnitude seismic activity - (due to specific patterns of locations in which they appear they could possibly predict the location of the next light). That may give the MTF a choice between choosing The Foundation or SCPs. I'd have to decide which they choose from there.<br />
This war could then tie in with the MTF which you mentioned attempting to neutralize the entities seemingly inside of an entire war between these light beings &amp; The Foundation. I'd have to choose how that ends, however. If they're capable of just shifting tectonic plates it could end in a possible XK-Class Scenario, ending the entire world, however I don't know if my first SCP would be allowed to go that far. I'll have to think about the escalation of it a bit more.</p>
<p>Reply to below, as I don't want to further the thread:</p>
<p>You saying that gave me another possible idea that the MTF is actually a &quot;spokesperson&quot; for the light people, and he advocates for the peace between them and delivers messages. I'll continue to think about it as much as I can, as it'd make sense the SCP Foundation wouldn't want to engage war.</p>

