<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">[Placeholder]</span></p>
<p>Hey, author, let's take a look.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Feedback</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Why they do this is found out in the tale.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm finding it hard to understand. Is this an SCP article or a Tale? It looks like you're focusing too much on the story instead of trying to explain what those entities are.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He gains motivation to learn more about them to try and find a way to have the foundation assist in this 'chaos'-addiction, as that's what he always wished he had. This also motivates him to write more so the foundation can understand as much as they can.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You have to keep in mind that The Foundation is cold, pratical and doesn't like to waste time. The only reason why they would try to help these entities is because they would gain some benefit through that. If there is one, you have to make that clear. Also, I believe that The Foundation would consider the MTF unit's opinion untrustworthy. Someone who's emotionally invested in something, specially a soldier, would have a different view of what something actually is. The Foundation would also not trust the entities, since they could also be lying. Just like a real drug addict, they could be trying to get even more chaos by destroying the SCP Foundation and releasing other SCPs across the world, and they would only gain benefit from it, since they live out of chaos.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These light creatures are entities born from dying stars, and as such are naturally attracted towards extremely chaotic events, living off of the chaos.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>We have some problems with this statement. First, I don't think an entity born from a dying star would be able to produce light, since the star is&#8230; well, dying, which means it's losing its ability to produce light. Second, considering that they are able to travel through space, Earth would be the worst place to go if they want extremely chaotic events. Compare a Supernova to an earthquake. Since they're attracted to destruction (and other similar things) and are capable of interplanetary travel, then they would definitely choose to go to another place in the universe to look for those events.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>As they're aware they would be unable to defeat these entities</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How so? Since you didn't describe the entity thoroughly, then there's no way of knowing why the foundation isn't able to damage this SCP.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;The&nbsp;actual&nbsp;idea</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So&#8230; This one has a little bit of potential, but it has a lot of flaws and unlogical things. Just like REDESERT 7 said, both the main character and the entities aren't really explored as they should be. You also need to inform us about the entities secrets and reasons to why they want to stay on Earth, since like I said before, there are better places to go if they want pure chaos. I really think that The Foundation wouldn't trust these entities at all, since all they do is gain strength through destruction, even though they don't want to do it, but The Foundation is basically enabling them. I think you should try to remodel the whole concept and think about something that could grab the reader's attention besides the usual &quot;powerful creature destroying stuff and feeding itself&quot;.</p>
<p>No greenlight for now. Good luck ;)</p>
</div>
